use "atlas-scripts-sml/Lattice.sml";

(*
  File: atlas-scripts-sml/unitary.sml

  Purpose
  - SML translation of `atlas-scripts/unitary.at`.
  - Provides hard-coded lists of rational weights (“ratvec” values) used in the
    Atlas script ecosystem as representatives of unitary facets / spherical
    unitary parameters for selected split groups.

  Notes on coordinates
  - `F4_spherical_unitary`: fundamental weight coordinates, with the Dynkin
    diagram reversed as in the original `.at` script.
  - `D4_spherical_unitary`: standard coordinates with `rho = (3,2,1,0)`.
  - `E7_spherical_unitary`: as in the original `.at` script (see the comments in
    `atlas-scripts/unitary.at` for provenance).

  Types
  - Each list element is a `Lattice.ratvec = {nums, den}` representing `nums/den`.

  Implementation detail
  - The helper `rv` normalizes each vector (gcd reduction and positive
    denominator), so the literal data matches the `.at` meaning even when the
    `.at` file uses per-coordinate fractions (e.g. `7/8`).
*)
